Put it after the elements (or use `defer`) so the IDs exist when the script runs.

```javascript
let clicks = 0;
document.getElementById('go').addEventListener('click', () => {
  clicks += 1;
  document.getElementById('out').textContent = 'Clicked ' + clicks + ' times';
});
```

Use a conditional: 

```javascript
const label = clicks === 1 ? 'time' : 'times';
document.getElementById('out').textContent = `Clicked ${clicks} ${label}`;
```

Yes: disable the button when the count reaches 5.

```javascript
const btn = document.getElementById('go');
btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  clicks += 1;
  const label = clicks === 1 ? 'time' : 'times';
  document.getElementById('out').textContent = `Clicked ${clicks} ${label}`;
  if (clicks >= 5) btn.disabled = true;
});
```

